{
  "headline": "Aprepitant is not on FDA's shortage list; supply traces to a plant classified OAI 152 days before the import alert",
  "headline_cites": ["D4", "E8", "E5", "E7", "D5"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include aprepitant as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 80 mg capsules used at Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside share NDC 51407070202 and label set 377c3ecb, which names Pharmathen International S. A. (FEI 3009961173) as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E3", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2025-11-21 and classified the inspection OAI, with the classification known to FDA on 2026-02-26.",
      "cites": ["E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An import alert (66-40) for the same firm and FEI was published on 2026-04-23, 152 days after the OAI inspection end date.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A warning letter was issued to the firm on 2026-05-27.",
      "cites": ["E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC lists aprepitant oral powder for suspension as to be discontinued with an initial posting date of 2026-04-08.",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked mitigation is to transfer 47 capsules of 80 mg from Corvale General (26.4 days on hand) to Corvale East (8.4 days on hand), which would bring Corvale East to 14 days of supply while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D5"]
    }
  ]
}
